# DATA_DIR (host bind mounts)

Default host directory for persistent Docker data on the **travis** home lab server:

```text
/home/travis/10-docker-data
```

## Compose

- Use `${DATA_DIR:-/home/travis/10-docker-data}` in volume paths (never `${DATA_DIR:-.}`).
- Subpaths: stack-specific names (e.g. `${LAB_FOLDER:-01-artex-llm}_postgres`, `postgres_data_${DEPLOY_ENV:-dev}`).
- Do not confuse with **in-container** env vars named `DATA_DIR` (e.g. app config under `/app/data`).

```yaml
volumes:
  - ${DATA_DIR:-/home/travis/10-docker-data}/${LAB_FOLDER:-01-artex-llm}_postgres:/var/lib/postgresql/data
```

## Env files

- `.env.example`: set `DATA_DIR=/home/travis/10-docker-data`.
- Local overrides only in untracked `.env` (e.g. `DATA_DIR=.` for laptop dev without that path).

## Dokploy

- Set `DATA_DIR` in compose environment when the Dokploy server is not travis (or rely on the compose default above).